FerrionOS change to upstream RedoxFS (MIT license, kept), made against upstream commit 5ba45a6887374ab425326656a276bb3b62eba7dc after the existing recipe patches. Found by the deterministic simulation in sim/redoxfs (sim/redoxfs/run.sh replay FILE runs a replay).

RedoxFS never asked the disk to make its writes durable, so a disk with a write cache could store a header before the blocks it points to, or lose a committed transaction. Disk gains flush (by default nothing), called after the data blocks and after the header of every commit; DiskFile syncs its data, DiskCache and Box<dyn Disk> pass it on, and DiskRing keeps its disk descriptor to fsync it. Disk drivers still have to turn that fsync into a cache flush.

Replay (seed 2): the first operation returns with 269 writes still in the simulated volatile cache. Without this patch 59 of 120 simulated seeds fail (every seed that simulates a write cache).
diff --git a/src/disk/cache.rs b/src/disk/cache.rs
index f3851ce..73b79dd 100644
--- a/src/disk/cache.rs
+++ b/src/disk/cache.rs
@@ -132,4 +132,8 @@ impl<T: Disk> Disk for DiskCache<T> {
     fn size(&mut self) -> Result<u64> {
         self.inner.size()
     }
+
+    fn flush(&mut self) -> Result<()> {
+        self.inner.flush()
+    }
 }
diff --git a/src/disk/file.rs b/src/disk/file.rs
index 8782e34..5124231 100644
--- a/src/disk/file.rs
+++ b/src/disk/file.rs
@@ -81,6 +81,10 @@ impl Disk for DiskFile {
